{"name":"Curtain Call","hex":"#70666a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"curtain call","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The moment at the end of a performance when actors come back on the stage and thank the audience for applauding them for their performance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curtain_call"}],"entries":[{"title":"Curtain call","blocks":[{"text":"A curtain call occurs at the end of a performance when one or more performers return to the stage to be recognized by the audience for the performance. In musical theatre, the performers typically recognize the orchestra and its conductor at the end of the curtain call. Luciano Pavarotti holds the record for receiving 165 curtain calls, more than any other artist, for his February 24, 1988, performance of Nemorino in Gaetano Donizetti's L'elisir d'amore."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Nightwish-Melbourne-2008.jpg/330px-Nightwish-Melbourne-2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curtain_call"},{"title":"Curtain Call (South Korean TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Curtain Call is a 2022 South Korean television series starring Kang Ha-neul, Ha Ji-won, Go Doo-shim, Sung Dong-il, Jung Ji-so, Noh Sang-hyun, and Kwon Sang-woo. The series revolves around a man who plays the role of a grandson who defected to fulfill his grandmother's last wish from the North, a woman who falls in love with that man, and the people involved in the play. It premiered on KBS2 on October 31, 2022, and aired every Monday and Tuesday at 21:50 (KST). It is also available for streaming on Amazon Prime Video in selected regions."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/68/Curtain_Call_%28South_Korean_TV_series%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curtain_Call_(South_Korean_TV_series)"},{"title":"Curtain","blocks":[{"text":"A curtain is a piece of cloth or other material intended to block or obscure light, air drafts, or water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Gordijnen_aan_venster.JPG/330px-Gordijnen_aan_venster.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curtain"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Curtain_call.jpg/500px-Curtain_call.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Curtain_call.jpg/1280px-Curtain_call.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Curtain_call.jpg/500px-Curtain_call.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Turandot directed by Roberto De Simone. January 2012, Teatro Comunale Bologna","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACurtain_call.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/39_Merci_Ars%C3%A8ne_-_Goodbye_Ars%C3%A8ne%21_%2841056012185%29.jpg/500px-39_Merci_Ars%C3%A8ne_-_Goodbye_Ars%C3%A8ne%21_%2841056012185%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/39_Merci_Ars%C3%A8ne_-_Goodbye_Ars%C3%A8ne%21_%2841056012185%29.jpg/1280px-39_Merci_Ars%C3%A8ne_-_Goodbye_Ars%C3%A8ne%21_%2841056012185%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/39_Merci_Ars%C3%A8ne_-_Goodbye_Ars%C3%A8ne%21_%2841056012185%29.jpg/500px-39_Merci_Ars%C3%A8ne_-_Goodbye_Ars%C3%A8ne%21_%2841056012185%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Arsène Wenger on the field of play at the conclusion of his final home game as m